{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 74","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_74&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on opposite sides of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the centroids of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/a/b2a8fd2178bc28fa82544c86b83d7abc47987127.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=841$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa6254ddd663cccc6d09a5027ded68dbae1e323.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=840$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca410f17b67161c696605fccede9a23738084cf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8ef7c1708de12065f4f545438d3dd66df2be8b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=609$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3e1368a423e0d9661eb0df1bbf04ac3f3547e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=580$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />, find the sum of the numerator and denominator of the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> when expressed as a fraction in lowest terms.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_74&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eaab6bc6c847d4a9e94c35d207bc57d662612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41^2 + 840^2 = 841^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/507759df6e21d58cafede0eecf0112b772ca8bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$580^2 + 609^2 = 841^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are right triangles. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/62928d44c93b55840811868458f3378a8673f654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = \\angle ADB = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"184\" height=\"13\" />, quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4ad0ca46478a16fbb3bfb9642319ae51c2c6da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACBD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_quadrilateral\" title=\"Cyclic quadrilateral\">cyclic</a>.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c82640e0e11f8ffd6da6860820b608829683f3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(0,0),C=(1681/841,34440/841),B=(841,0),D=(370881/841,-353220/841); draw(A--C--B--D--A); dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,W); dot(C); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,NW); dot(B); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,E); dot(D); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,S);  draw(circle((841/2,0),841/2)); dot((841/2,0)); draw(C--(841/2,0)--D);  pair M=(1417924/5046,11480/841),n=(1282/3,-140);  dot(M); dot(n); label(&quot;M&quot;,M,N); label(&quot;N&quot;,n,E);  draw(C--D,dotted); draw(M--n,dotted); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"228\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Centroid\" title=\"Centroid\">centroids</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cadf13a94450bcd60eb35ca604e1818d45cbd9ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM : MO = DN : DO = 2 : 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"241\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, by SAS Similarity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a90d153fe4839e477a4d998274855acc54278cb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle COD \\sim \\triangle MON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb1b154e2883ab15931ab1e336605fd24623e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = \\tfrac13 CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s Theorem\">Ptolemy's Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8ca3619c550790bab2401897f6b6ceacaa177446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\cdot BD + BC \\cdot AD = CD \\cdot AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"259\" height=\"14\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92ff5d2295e1fc3285ba2e28ae089d72d5b505b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 41 \\cdot 580 + 840 \\cdot 609 &amp;= 841 \\cdot CD \\\\ 535340 &amp;= 841 \\cdot CD \\\\ CD &amp;= \\frac{18460}{29} \\end{align*}\" width=\"242\" height=\"86\" />\n</p><p>That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b72d9624dd287d9e8458743573a197a99154295b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = \\tfrac13 \\cdot \\tfrac{18460}{29} = \\tfrac{18460}{87}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"181\" height=\"21\" />, and the sum of the numerator and denominator in lowest terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f1f372250830ec4af2012e142fd08f0860f799d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18460 + 87 = \\boxed{18547}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_74&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_73\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 73\">Problem 73</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_75\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 75\">Problem 75</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Pro